  "observations": [
    "Installed spawner type is DefaultBattleMissionAgentSpawnLogic; older MissionAgentSpawnLogic names did not match metadata.",
    "MaxNumberOfAgentsForMission lazily caches IMBAgent.GetMaximumNumberOfAgents(); managed code does not establish that native returned value.",
    "MaxNumberOfTroopsForMission is integer MaxNumberOfAgentsForMission / 2.",
    "NumberOfAgents is Mission.AllAgents.Count.",
    "GetReservedTroopQuota returns 2 when spawning horses and reserved troop IsMounted; otherwise returns 1.",
    "TryReinforcementSpawn checks MaxNumberOfAgentsForMission - NumberOfAgents >= GetReservedTroopQuota(0) before spawning one troop.",
    "Mission.OnAgentRemoved removes the agent from _activeAgents but not _allAgents.",
    "Mission.OnAgentDeleted notifies behavior callbacks before removing the agent from _allAgents.",
    "Mission.BuildAgent appends each built agent to both active and all agent lists; SpawnAgent builds mount and human separately.",
    "CustomBattleMissionSpawnHandler.AfterStart enables horses on both sides and initializes default single-phase spawning.",
    "Agent.FadeOut forwards to native IMBAgent.FadeOut; requested mounted fade invokes FadeOut on MountAgent too."
  ],
  "inferences": [
    "Use AllAgents plus in-flight spawn reservations for capacity accounting; do not release allocation merely on killed/removed callbacks.",
    "Reconcile capacity on a subsequent tick after deletion callback to avoid stale list counts.",
    "A standalone virtual-army demo should own its spawner or explicitly replace the default spawn lifecycle; adding a second spawner to vanilla handler risks duplicate troops and inconsistent victory/accounting.",
    "Separate virtual soldier identity from native Agent.Index; native slot reuse and lifetime are not virtual identity.",
    "Safest initial demonstration is bounded detailed infantry with NoHorses(true), immutable cohort state, and no campaign outcome integration until verified."
  ],
